  "scope": "private S3-output stock runtime gates; GUI and independent Phase02/03 regressions remain separate",
  "coverage_notes": "AC-5 requires actual stock echo nonzero exits with missing stdout, stderr or both; invalid stdout refs must be rejected by canonical admission before publication, recorded distinctly from helper execution. All negative cases require empty owned streams, no unrelated host bytes, and independent no-UART-payload checks.\nAC-4 fragmented stock ls writes use 60-byte names and separate LF across full 4096-byte rings; exact retained bytes are checked, but internal write return counts are not externally exposed and are not independently observed.\ndate/env/uname/kill/shutdown/hotswap are signed and packaged but NOT launched: no broadened target admission, authority, shutdown or service mutation.\nS2-N: denial of Resolve/TcpConnect/UdpCreate/UdpBind/TcpListen/MulticastJoin/L2Send is observed as Err(0xFC) by a no-rights Cell; the unchanged net socket count is a host-test claim (service-net), not observed here. curl admission is observed as a network failure (no response) on restricted SLIRP; no data transfer is claimed.\nS2-T/S2-W: a telemetry refusal is observed as the syscall ABI's single generic error return (PermissionDenied is not distinguishable on the wire), so the same binary on its /bin fixture row must read rows for each call; the VFS refusal is Err(ERR_DENIED) to WriteAt through the delegated cwd handle. The kernel CapSet values themselves are host-test claims, not observed here.\nS5-3 option C: the shell's Lost(4)/FrontendAttached observations are its own fixed UART log lines; frontend holder death (resume revoked, Lost(4) then EOF) is not exercised because the holder is the driver itself; it is an input host-test claim here.\nS5-4a: the driver is the frontend, so no terminal emulator is in this loop: hostile output is judged as the exact relayed bytes plus the absence of any injected shell input (the next command's exact echo, history = typed lines only); screen effects are the GUI runner's claim. read -s: the token is typed 1.5 s after the command line, after the shell took its echo-off lease (the lease itself is not externally observable here). The physical-UART refusal of read -s is judged by the Phase02 serial runner.\nS6-5: TCG with one vCPU; every CPU threshold (D65-6) and every compared value is recorded as P04 INFO top-load, no CPU-speed or hardware claim follows. The same-snapshot numeric TUI = batch = records proof stays the constructed host pair (D64-14); here the views are compared on membership. top's own truncation rendering is host-tested; the runtime claim is the provider's explicit truncation (s2tw-probe trunc). Allocation failures, watchdog kills and faults during the load scenarios are judged by the log-wide no-OOM/no-panic checks and by both fixtures surviving to `bye` with status 0.\n",
